# Dack Fayden, Helping Hand in a game of three: X is two, so two creature cards are revealed - each past a land, which
# stays in the library - put onto the battlefield together under Bot1's control, then shuffled and goaded. Bot1 chooses
# Bot2 for the first of them; the second must go to a different opponent, so Bot3 has it, with no question asked. In a
# game of more than two the player who goes first draws on turn 1 (CR 103.8a), so the Forest is in hand by turn 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Dack Fayden, Helping Hand
Island
Island
Forest
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island
Llanowar Elves
Island x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dack Fayden, Helping Hand.Cast
Bot1.ChoosePlayer(Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Bot1.Library.Count = 11
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island; Island
Bot1.Battlefield = Dack Fayden, Helping Hand; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire
Bot2.Battlefield = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.GoadedBy = Bot1
Bot3.Battlefield = Llanowar Elves
Bot3.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.GoadedBy = Bot1
